    {
      "text": "I don't know what it is about laundry day, but it always gets me thinking. Maybe it's the quiet hum of the machine or the smell of detergent, but somehow I end up having a full-on life reflection while matching socks. I started off just trying to get through it, you know, get it done and move on with my day. But then halfway through folding, my brain's like, \"Hey, remember that embarrassing thing you said three years ago?\" And suddenly, I'm reliving random moments while folding a T-shirt. It's funny though. Each pile of clothes has its own little story. That shirt I wore when I met someone new, the hoodie I basically lived in last month, or the jeans that always shrink no matter what the tag says. By the end, I'm kind of in this weird calm mood, like somehow I sorted my thoughts along with the laundry. So yeah, laundry day might not be exciting, but it's not just about clean clothes. It's a mini therapy session, just you, your thoughts, and a mountain of socks that still refuse to match.",
      "start_time": 0.099,
      "end_time": 60.24,
